              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "жёлтый (zhyóltyy) — \"yellow\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "жёлтый (zhyóltyy) from Proto-Slavic žĭltŭ — inherited. Vasmer relates it to Lithuanian geltas, \"yellow\", Greek cholḗ, \"bile\", and Latin fel, \"bile\": bile was named for its colour. желчь, \"bile\", is its Russian twin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
