              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "плохой (plokhóy) from Old Russian ploxŭ, \"bad\"; Ukrainian плохий means \"meek, quiet\", and Polish płochy, \"timid\". Vasmer links it with переполох, \"a fright\", while others relate it to плоский, \"flat\", so the origin is not settled."
